f events `{ events: [...] }`\n  - All events associated with user's tenant\n  - Returns array of created event IDs\n  - **Verify**: all events stored, count increases\n- [ ] Events with missing `name` return 400\n- [ ] Events with empty events array return 400\n\n## 4. Query Engine (`/api/queries`)\n- [ ] `GET /api/queries/count?name=...&startDate=...&endDate=...` — count events matching filter\n  - Only returns count for user's tenant\n  - **Verify**: returns correct count, tenant-isolated\n- [ ] `GET /api/queries/timeseries?name=...&startDate=...&endDate=...&bucket=day|hour` — bucketed counts\n  - Returns array of `{ date, count }` objects\n  - **Verify**: correct bucketing, empty buckets included as 0\n- [ ] `GET /api/queries/breakdown?name=...&property=...&startDate=...&endDate=...` — breakdown by property\n  - Returns array of `{ value, count }` objects\n  - **Verify**: correct grouping by JSON property value, tenant-isolated\n\n## 5. Dashboard Configuration (`/api/dashboards`)\n- [ ] `GET /api/dashboards` — list dashboards for user's tenant\n  - **Verify**: only returns dashboards from user's tenant\n- [ ] `POST /api/dashboards` — create dashboard with `{ name, config? }`\n  - **Verify**: dashboard created with correct tenant_id\n- [ ] `GET /api/dashboards/:id` — get single dashboard\n  - **Verify**: returns dashboard, 404 if not found or wrong tenant\n- [ ] `PUT /api/dashboards/:id` — update dashboard name/config\n  - **Verify**: fields updated, updated_at changes\n- [ ] `DELETE /api/dashboards/:id` — delete dashboard\n  - **Verify**: deleted, subsequent GET returns 404\n\n### Widgets (sub-resources of dashboards)\n- [ ] `POST /api/dashboards/:id/widgets` — add widget `{ type, config?, position_x?, position_y?, width?, height? }`\n  - Type must be one of: counter, timeseries, breakdown, funnel\n  - **Verify**: widget created under dashboard\n- [ ] `PUT /api/dashboards/:dashboard_id/widgets/:widget_id` — update widget\n- [ ] `DELETE /api/dashboards/:dashboard_id/widgets/:widget_id` — delete widget\n- [ ] Widget routes enforce tenant boundaries via dashboard ownership\n\n## 6. Data Export (`/api/exports`)\n- [ ] `GET /api/exports/events?format=json` — export events as JSON array\n  - **Verify**: returns JSON, tenant-scoped\n- [ ] `GET /api/exports/events?format=csv` — export events as CSV\n  - **Verify**: returns CSV with headers, tenant-scoped\n  - CSV should include id, name, properties, timestamp, session_id\n- [ ] `GET /api/exports/dashboards/:id?format=json` — export dashboard as JSON\n- [ ] `GET /api/exports/dashboards/:id?format=csv` — export dashboard as CSV\n  - **Verify**: tenant-scoped, 404 if not found\n\n## 7. Authentication & Authorization\n- [ ] All routes except `POST /api/auth/register` and `POST /api/auth/login` require auth\n- [ ] Missing/invalid JWT returns 401 with `{ error, code }`\n- [ ] JWT payload shape is `{ sub, tid, role, iat, exp }`\n- [ ] Tenant isolation enforced: users only see their own tenant's data\n- [ ] Admin-only routes (role change) return 403 for non-admins\n\n## 8. Error Handling\n- [ ] All errors return `{ error, code }` JSON format\n- [ ] 400 for validation errors\n- [ ] 401 for authentication errors\n- [ ] 403 for authorization errors\n- [ ] 404 for not found\n- [ ] Unhandled errors return 500 with `{ error, code }`\n\n## Verification\n- [ ] `npm run build` — compiles cleanly\n- [ ] `npm run lint` — no lint errors\n- [ ] `npm run test` — all tests pass\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":24832,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0824a419-2aa7-4301-a54e-df3478f41e45","uuid":"e960fb99-c439-460b-b59a-31e37d3de966"}
